ype":"text_delta","text":" 65 or ta"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"king several"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" medications"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\nIf you have"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" symptoms like black"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" or"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" b"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"loody stools, v"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"omiting bl"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ood, sever"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"e st"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"omach pain, or y"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"ellowing sk"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"in or eyes, st"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"op ta"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"king them"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" and get"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" medical care"},{"type":"text_delta","text":"."},{"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"opaque","provider":"anthropic","kind":"thinking","data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"type":"text","text":"Yes, for most healthy adults, taking ibuprofen and acetaminophen together is generally considered safe. They work differently (ibuprofen is an NSAID that reduces inflammation, and acetaminophen is a pain and fever reliever), so they're sometimes combined or alternated for pain that isn't controlled by one alone. Some guidance:\n\n- **Stick to label doses and daily maximums for each.** Check that you're not doubling up on acetaminophen through cold, flu, or \"PM\" products.\n- **Use the shortest time needed.** If you need them for more than a few days, check with a doctor.\n- **Take ibuprofen with food** to lower the risk of stomach upset.\n\nAsk a doctor or pharmacist first if you:\n\n- Have kidney, liver, heart, or stomach/ulcer problems, or a history of GI bleeding\n- Have high blood pressure, heart failure, or take blood thinners, ACE inhibitors, ARBs, diuretics, or lithium\n- Drink alcohol regularly (this raises the risk of liver damage from acetaminophen and stomach bleeding from ibuprofen)\n- Are pregnant, or are giving medicine to a child (dosing is by weight)\n- Are over 65 or taking several medications\n\nIf you have symptoms like black or bloody stools, vomiting blood, severe stomach pain, or yellowing skin or eyes, stop taking them and get medical care."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":4517,"cache_creation_input_tokens":94},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
